                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Article 15 of the pharmacy regulations.</hi></head>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Art.</hi> 15. Permission for the sale of medicines or
                    galenic or compound drugs from abroad shall be applied for by a professor of
                    medicine or pharmacy by means of a memorial, accompanied by the medicine whose
                    introduction is desired and by two copies of the pharmacopoeia, formulary, work,
                    or periodical publication of medicine or pharmacy in which its composition
                    appears. A decision on such applications shall be preceded by a report from the
                    royal academy of medical, physical, and natural sciences of Habana and by an
                    opinion of the supreme board of health.</p>
            </div>
